Sure! Below is a simple example of a “card” that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
body { margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background:#f0f0f0; }

/* Container that holds the card – center it on the page */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Needed for 3D transform */
    margin: 80px auto;            /* Center horizontally + some top spacing */
}

/* The actual card element */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Keep children in 3D space */
    cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate around Y‑axis */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front side of the card */
.front, .back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;     /* Hide backside when rotated */
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Front styling */
.front {
    background: #fff;
    display:flex;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    font-size:1.5rem;
    color:#333;
}

/* Back styling – rotated 180° so it shows after flip */
.back {
    background: #4a90e2;
    color:white;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);       /* Flip it so it appears correctly */
    display:flex;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    font-size:1.2rem;
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">Front Side</div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">Back Side</div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Property | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `perspective` | Gives depth to the container so the 3D rotation looks realistic. |
| `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements in 3D space during transformation. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the reverse side of each face while rotating. |
| `transition` | Animates the rotation smoothly. |
| `rotateY(180deg)` | Rotates the card 180 degrees along the Y‑axis. |

Feel free to replace the text or add images inside `.front` and `.back`. You can also tweak colors, sizes, or add more complex content. Enjoy your rotating card!
